  "module_type": "standard",
  "question_text": "In the figure, triangle ABC has side BC lying along line n. Line m passes through vertex A and is parallel to line n. Point D lies on line m, on the opposite side of line AB from point C, and the measure of angle DAB is 48\u00b0. The measure of angle ACB is 67\u00b0. What is the measure, in degrees, of angle BAC?",
  "answer_a": "48",
  "answer_b": "65",
  "answer_c": "113",
  "answer_d": "115",
  "correct_answer": "B",
  "explanation": "Choice B is correct. Lines m and n are parallel and line AB is a transversal. Angle DAB and angle ABC are alternate interior angles, so they are congruent. It's given that the measure of angle DAB is 48\u00b0, so the measure of angle ABC is 48\u00b0. The sum of the measures of the interior angles of a triangle is 180\u00b0. Therefore, the measure of angle BAC is 180\u00b0 - 48\u00b0 - 67\u00b0 = 65\u00b0.",
  "distractor_a_explanation": "Choice A is incorrect. This is the measure of angle ABC, not angle BAC.",
  "distractor_b_explanation": "",
  "distractor_c_explanation": "Choice C is incorrect. This results from subtracting only the measure of angle ACB from 180\u00b0 (180 - 67 = 113) and not also subtracting the measure of angle ABC.",
  "distractor_d_explanation": "Choice D is incorrect. This is the sum of the measures of angle ABC and angle ACB (48 + 67 = 115), which is the measure of the exterior angle at A, not the measure of angle BAC.",
  "is_diagnostic": false,
  "is_active": true,
  "has_visual": true,
