  "difficulty": 1,
  "module_type": "standard",
  "question_text": "A loading ramp is supported by a vertical side panel in the shape of a right triangle. The ramp itself is the hypotenuse of the panel and makes a 30\u00b0 angle with the level ground. The panel's vertical side is 4 feet tall, as shown. A trim strip will be run along the entire outer edge of the panel, covering all three sides. What is the total length, in feet, of the trim strip?",
  "answer_a": "4 + 4\u221a3",
  "answer_b": "8 + 4\u221a3",
  "answer_c": "12 + 4\u221a3",
  "answer_d": "12 + 8\u221a3",
  "correct_answer": "C",
  "explanation": "Choice C is correct. The side panel is a right triangle with a 30\u00b0 angle, so its other acute angle is 60\u00b0, and it is a 30\u00b0-60\u00b0-90\u00b0 triangle. In such a triangle, the side opposite the 30\u00b0 angle is the shortest side, and the sides are in the ratio 1 : \u221a3 : 2. The vertical side is opposite the 30\u00b0 angle at the ground, so it is the short side, which is 4 feet. The ramp (hypotenuse) is 2(4) = 8 feet, and the horizontal side along the ground is 4\u221a3 feet. The trim strip covers all three sides, so its length is 4 + 4\u221a3 + 8 = 12 + 4\u221a3 feet.",
  "distractor_a_explanation": "Choice A is incorrect. This is the sum of the two legs, 4 + 4\u221a3, and leaves out the 8-foot ramp (the hypotenuse).",
  "distractor_b_explanation": "Choice B is incorrect. This is the sum of the ramp and the horizontal side, 8 + 4\u221a3, and leaves out the 4-foot vertical side.",
  "distractor_c_explanation": "",
  "distractor_d_explanation": "Choice D is incorrect. This results from applying the factor \u221a3 to the hypotenuse instead of to the short side, giving a horizontal side of 8\u221a3 rather than 4\u221a3, so the sum is 4 + 8\u221a3 + 8 = 12 + 8\u221a3.",
